---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/base.astro";

const updated = "2026-11-14";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How the Ladybird Browser Initiative handles your information."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero__tf">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="single-content">
    <div class="container">
      <p>
        Ladybird Browser Initiative doesn't track your browsing or sell your
        data. This policy covers the browser, our website, newsletter,
        donations, and correspondence.
      </p>

      <h2>Crash reports</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to send a report, we use it to find and fix bugs. Reports
        contain technical details about your Ladybird build, operating system,
        and crash, including an error message and stack trace. You can also
        choose to include the URL of the page that crashed and a description of
        what happened. We keep reports and submission IP addresses for up to 93
        days, then delete them. We use the IP addresses to limit spam.
      </p>

      <h2>Site compatibility reports</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to send a report, we receive your description of the
        problem, the page URL, technical information about your Ladybird build
        and system, a screenshot unless you remove it, and, if you choose,
        layout and painting information. These can show what's on the page, such
        as your name or messages if you are signed in, so check them before
        sending. We use these reports to investigate and fix compatibility
        problems. If we accept a report, we publish its contents, except your IP
        address, as a public issue on GitHub, where it stays visible. Parts of
        it may also be posted to our Discord server. We keep other reports for
        up to 93 days, then delete them.
      </p>

      <h2>Updates and downloads</h2>
      <p>
        When a Ladybird build from us checks for updates, it sends your Ladybird
        version and platform. Downloads, updates, and packages from us are
        delivered through Cloudflare, which also receives your IP address when
        you connect.
      </p>

      <h2>Features you turn on</h2>
      <p>
        Some features contact other services only if you turn them on. Filter
        lists, such as EasyList, are downloaded and updated from their
        maintainers' servers. Search suggestions send what you type in the
        address bar to your chosen search engine. Those services receive your IP
        address and handle it under their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Website</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is served through Cloudflare and hosted on GitHub Pages,
        which process connection information, including your IP address, to
        deliver and protect the site. The site doesn't use cookies or analytics.
        Logs we retain for our own online services are kept for up to 93 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us, we keep your message for as long as it's useful for
        responding to you and keeping a record of our work. You can ask us to
        delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Donations</h2>
      <p>
        If you donate, we receive donor and transaction information from the
        service you use. We use it to manage donations, send receipts, and keep
        financial records. We keep financial records for as long as US tax and
        nonprofit law requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe, we use your email address to send Ladybird updates.
        Our newsletter provider also stores subscription details, including your
        signup date, IP address, and referrer information. Email tracking is
        disabled. You can unsubscribe at any time. We keep subscription records
        while you're subscribed. After you unsubscribe, a record remains to
        prevent accidental resubscription; you can ask us to delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        We use external services for hosting, email, newsletters, and donations.
        Our <a href="/service-providers/">Service providers</a> page explains which
        services we use and what they handle.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ladybird Browser Initiative is based in the United States, so
        information you send us is processed there.
      </p>

      <h2>Your information</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or requests to access, correct, or delete your
        information, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@ladybird.org">privacy@ladybird.org</a>.
        Depending on the law that applies, you can also request a portable copy,
        object to or restrict processing, withdraw consent, and complain to a
        data protection authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ladybird Browser Initiative<br />
        2261 Market Street STE 10029<br />
        San Francisco, CA 94114-1612<br />
        United States
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use this information</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on your consent to send newsletters and process voluntary crash
        and compatibility reports. We use connection details and update checks
        to operate, update, and protect our services, and keep correspondence to
        handle your inquiries. These are our legitimate interests. We keep
        financial records to meet our legal obligations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero__tf .updated {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
